2,Leeward Caribbean English Creole Language... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/aig/,"Leeward Caribbean English Creole is a stable indigenous language of Antigua and Barbuda, Anguilla, Montserrat, Saint Kitts and Nevis, and Saint Martin. It is an English-based creole.",Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
3,"Full text of ""enwiki-Leeward_Caribbean_Creole_English-20200726.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/enwiki-Leeward_Caribbean_Creole_English-20200726.pdf/enwiki-Leeward_Caribbean_Creole_English-20200726_djvu.txt,Leeward Caribbean Creole English first emerged during the 18th century as an English-lexifer Creole.^ While it thus adopted many features of the English language everything from the creole's lexicon to its phonology reflects Antigua's more nuanced history.,Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
4,Official Languages of the 13 Caribbean Countries,https://www.energy.co.kr:455/news/the-main-languages-of-the-13-caribbean-countries.html,Primary Spoken Language: Antiguan and Barbudan Creole (Leeward Caribbean Creole English). It's an English-based creole that is the default for casual conversation among locals.,Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
