6,English is the official language of Antigua and Barbuda.,https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/what-languages-are-spoken-in-antigua-and-barbuda.html,"Antigua and Barbuda Creole English. As many of the residents in this country are descendants of African slaves, the common English spoken in this country has been influenced by African words and phrases.",Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
7,Leeward Caribbean English Creole Translator | Free & AI-Powered,https://anythingtranslate.com/translators/leeward-caribbean-english-creole-translator/,"Leeward Caribbean English Creole. Or upload image.This unique language, a beautiful blend of English and Creole influences, brings the spirit of the islands to life with its lively phrases and rhythmic flow.",Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
8,What is the Language Spoken in Antigua? (Essential...) - edupark.blog,https://edupark.blog/language-spoken-antigua,"While Standard English is used for government, commerce, and media, the vast majority of the population speaks Antiguan Creole (also known as Leeward Caribbean Creole English) in daily life. This unique linguistic blend reflects the island's colonial history and its rich African heritage.",Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
9,What language is spoken in Antigua and Barbuda?,https://citizenx.com/insights/antigua-barbuda-language/,"While English is the official language, many locals speak Antiguan and Barbudan Creole, also known as Leeward Caribbean Creole English. This creole language is a unique blend of English with African and other influences, reflecting the islands' rich cultural tapestry.",Leeward Caribbean English Creole,Creole
